      "author_association": "MEMBER",
      "body": "That's not the right approach. FP4 needs FP32 due to cuDNN kernel limitation, but MXFP8 does not have such issue. So the right fix should be to cast only when use_nvfp4 is True and leave the type of the scales unchanged (either BF16 or FP32), depending on what type we got.",
      "commit_id": "3855c1677542dba62ea6211455f0288614484257",
      "created_at": "2026-10-09T23:47:23Z",
      "diff_hunk": "@@ -1610,9 +1610,8 @@ def fuser_forward(\n \n         fc1_prob_tensor = None\n         if not unit_activation_scale:\n-            fc1_prob_tensor = (\n-                scales.detach().to(dtype=torch.float32 if use_nvfp4 else dtype).reshape(-1, 1, 1)\n-            )\n+            # Match the FP32 probabilities used by activation recomputation in backward.\n+            fc1_prob_tensor = scales.detach().to(dtype=torch.float32).reshape(-1, 1, 1)",
      "html_url": "https://github.com/NVIDIA/TransformerEngine/pull/3653#discussion_r4235459287",
