      "author_association": "CONTRIBUTOR",
      "body": "<!-- greptile_summary -->\n\n<h2><a href=\"https://app.greptile.com/api/retrigger?id=77255395\"><picture><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: dark)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/RetriggerDark.svg?v=2\"><source media=\"(prefers-color-scheme: light)\" srcset=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\"><img alt=\"Retrigger\" src=\"https://greptile-static-assets.s3.amazonaws.com/badges/Retrigger.svg?v=2\" align=\"right\"></picture></a>Confidence Score: 5/5</h2>\n\n**[Medium risk]** Adjusts numerical precision in grouped MLP router probability calculations\\.\n\nThe PR appears safe to merge; no actionable issues were found.\n\nWhat we checked:\n- Probability gradients keep their dtype: The forward pass saves the original `scales` tensor. The backward pass casts `grad_scales` to `scales.dtype`, and the fuser returns it without another cast.\n\n<h3>Summary</h3>\n\nPreserves router probability precision in fused grouped MLPs.\n- Forward kernels now receive FP32 probabilities for both MXFP8 and NVFP4.\n- Probability gradients return in the original probability dtype.\n- Adds numerical and exact-value regression checks for SReLU, tanh-SReLU, and SwiGLU.\n- No actionable issues found. GPU tests were not run.\n\n<h3>Diagram</h3>\n\n```mermaid\n%%{init: {'theme': 'neutral'}}%%\nflowchart LR\n  P[Original router probabilities] --> F[Convert to FP32 for forward]\n  P --> S[Save original probabilities]\n  S --> B[FP32 backward reduction]\n  B --> G[Cast gradient to original probability dtype]\n```\n\n<!-- greptile_confidence_score:5 -->\n\n<sub>Reviews (1) · Last reviewed commit: [\"Preserve router probability precision in...\"](https://github.com/nvidia/transformerengine/commit/3855c1677542dba62ea6211455f0288614484257) · [Reviewed by Greptile](https://www.greptile.com/?utm_source=greptile_expert&utm_medium=github&utm_campaign=code_reviews&utm_content=nvidia/transformerengine)</sub>",
